[[0,525416,0,17,3,14,"2015-09-19T18:23:15","Evrocot","",[],"","Glock with extended clip","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h3WXNIl_6jg","videos"],[1,2503640,0,2,0,2,"2015-09-19T18:33:18","CANCEL-CAT-FACTS","",[],"<p>He bought this at the Back to School sale.</p>"],[1,2503828,0,13,0,13,"2015-09-19T18:49:20","wafflecopter9001","",[],"<blockquote>\n<p>clip</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"http://i0.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/newsfeed/000/811/350/af0.gif\">Triggering intensifies</a></p>"],[2,2505202,2503828,2,0,2,"2015-09-19T20:58:50","Link1299","",[],"<p>plebs calling gun magazines &quot;clips&quot; <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/sRWv2T4.jpg\">http://i.imgur.com/sRWv2T4.jpg</a></p>"],[1,2503835,0,1,0,1,"2015-09-19T18:49:58","DoctorShitlord_MD","",[],"<p>Where can I get one</p>"],[1,2504409,0,6,0,6,"2015-09-19T19:43:44","SenatorYeezus","",[],"<p>I will take this opportunity to explain the difference between a clip and a magazine. A magazine has a spring which feeds ammunition to the firearm, whereas a clip does not.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magazine_%28firearms%29\">Magazines in detail</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clip_%28firearms%29\">clips in detail</a>.</p>"],[1,2504667,0,0,0,0,"2015-09-19T20:09:30","NedTaggart","",[],"<blockquote>\n<p>&lt; </p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Here we go</p>"],[1,2505178,0,0,0,0,"2015-09-19T20:56:52","Link1299","[e]",[],"<p>Fun Fact: how the glock's firing mechanism is designed, you can do something called &quot;bump firing&quot; in which you use the trigger guard and recoil of the gun to repeatedly fire a semi-automatic glock in an automatic way </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tHYZp8UEEzg\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tHYZp8UEEzg</a></p>\n<p>it however is both ineffective at proper gun control and requires a bump stock and is more of a neat trick than anything else</p>"],[1,2506687,0,0,0,0,"2015-09-19T23:16:53","Moderately_soluble","",[],"<p>Wow, that's shooting an entire 30 round magazine clip in 2 seconds</p>"]]
